# SO 251.826: is it CH3OH A-ladder?
res[69]['value']=res[69]['value'].replace("UNCONFIRMED.","UNCONFIRMED and BLENDED with CH3OH (round 4).",1)+". Round-4 blend test (scripts/s24_so_251826.py, Xb4f, template-shift vs HCO+ 3-2): feature centred at -28+-12 km/s from HCO+ (S) and -36+-15 (Bridge) if it is SO 251.8257 (2.3-2.4 sigma); if it is the CH3OH A-type 3(3)-2(2)...6(3)-6(2) ladder (251.74-251.92, Eu 64-99 K) the offset is +47+-12 (S) at Tex 10 K weights (3.9 sigma) or +23+-12 (1.9 sigma) at 25 K weights. Predicted CH3OH ladder integral relative to the CH3OH 254.015 line (LTE, S, I254=0.59 Jy/beam km/s): 0.10 Jy/beam km/s at Tex=10 K (~35% of the observed 0.28), 0.61 at 15 K (all of it), 2.8 at 25 K (excluded by the J>=4 blend limits); with the 254/blend ratio giving Tex 8-21 K the ladder can account for 0-100% of the 251.83 GHz feature. The SO flux is therefore an upper limit (<=0.28+-0.06 Jy/beam km/s at S) and SO is not available as a shock tracer; centroid slightly favours SO over a hot (Tex>=20 K) CH3OH ladder"
